ely whether the Tenant CRD can carry the configurable group claim path in the baseline, with the fallback documented if frozen.\n- The report states definitively whether maas-api observability instrumentation is feasible in-tree for the baseline, with the post-3.4 patch or deferral recommendation if not.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping — feasibility gate\n- [P0] Observability metrics functional — feasibility gate\n- Dependency: MaaS 3.4 GA codebase (internal, \"critical blocker\" for Summit timeline)\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":52590,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab07d7148cbf06fc","agent_id":"a5dd9ebccf03d402c","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4feb-9959-cd45ee4b4e7a","uuid":"a674a164-f57d-439d-ad71-58ecd1533b0f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:55:07.204Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003"}
