{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-a514073e-2178-4d08-af2b-fddf47224945","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-91443eef537a4cf5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-oimz6d8o/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-E004.md","content":"# MaaS Helm Chart Packaging for xKS\n\n## Description\n\nPackages the MaaS components (maas-api, maas-controller, payload-processing BBR ext_proc server) as Helm charts for deployment on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (xKS), replacing the OLM-based operator installation used on RHOAI. This is the foundational packaging work that all xKS deployment validation builds against.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Helm charts for maas-api, maas-controller, and the payload-processing ext_proc server, built from the existing deployment manifests (architecture context: models-as-a-service.md, deployment/base).\n- Configurable chart values for:\n  - Gateway class name (Istio `GatewayClass` for CKS as priority platform; other validated options such as `envoy-gateway` for multi-platform and `azure-application-gateway` for AKS)\n  - OIDC issuer configuration (issuer URL, client ID, audience, group claim path) for tenants that configure external OIDC\n  - TLS certificate source via cert-manager (replacing OpenShift service-CA auto-generated certificates)\n  - PostgreSQL connection, supporting either a shared (with other RHAII components) or dedicated instance\n  - Group claim path mapping value\n- Remove OpenShift-specific installation assumptions (no OLM; no `openshift-default` GatewayClass requirement) while keeping RHOAI deployments unaffected (additive/configuration-driven per the strategy's backwards-compatibility NFR).\n- The existing Gateway API HTTPRoutes are GatewayClass-agnostic per architecture context, so routing manifests carry over with configurable gateway/parent references.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a non-OpenShift Kubernetes cluster with a supported Gateway API implementation installed, when the MaaS Helm chart is installed with values set for that platform's gateway class, then maas-api, maas-controller, and payload-processing pods are running and healthy, measured by pod readiness checks passing.\n- TLS certificates are issued via cert-manager and served on the MaaS API endpoints, measured by successful TLS handshake validation.\n- The PostgreSQL connection is configurable for both shared and dedicated instances, measured by successful chart installation against each mode (resolves the shared-vs-dedicated open question as a configuration value, not a code change).\n- Chart values expose the OIDC issuer and group claim path configuration surface used by the external OIDC authentication capability.\n- Build pipeline for the Helm chart artifacts is green (the strategy's build onboarding prerequisite is satisfied for the chart).\n- RHOAI MaaS GA deployments are unchanged by this work (no regression to the OLM-based path).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] MaaS successfully deployed on CKS (packaging prerequisite)\n- [P0] MaaS successfully deployed on AKS (packaging prerequisite)\n- Out-of-scope confirmation: operator-based installation on xKS is excluded (Helm only per RFE)\n\n## Risks\n\n- Helm chart build pipeline onboarding is a pending human-review prerequisite in the strategy; if the review requires dedicated pipeline work, a follow-up epic may be needed.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":56278,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab07d7148cbf06fc","agent_id":"a5dd9ebccf03d402c","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4feb-9959-cd45ee4b4e7a","uuid":"07d5e817-e09e-47f2-951f-c74ee406d71f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:55:37.702Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003"}
