{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-9340b9e3-7e96-4eb3-a88f-b7fe94795fc9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-aed0e4c3ef824d4f","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-oimz6d8o/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-E007.md","content":"# MaaS Deployment Validation on CKS\n\n## Description\n\nDeploys the MaaS 3.4 baseline on CKS (CoreWeave Kubernetes Service) — the priority platform per Staff Engineer Input — via the Helm-based installation, and validates core MaaS functionality: subscription/tier management, token rate limiting, API key authentication, and external OIDC authentication. Produces the documented engineering delta and known-limitations list for MaaS on xKS versus RHOAI MaaS GA.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Deploy MaaS (maas-api, maas-controller, payload-processing) on a CKS test cluster via the Helm chart, using the Istio GatewayClass with appropriate TLS and mTLS configuration for Istio's control plane integration.\n- Deploy Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) on CKS via the deployment mechanism selected by the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS deployment path investigation (official RHCL Helm charts, or standalone Authorino + Limitador Helm as fallback).\n- Configure a customer-style external OIDC identity provider (OIDC-compatible, e.g. Keycloak-class) and exercise user authentication end to end.\n- Validate core functionality: subscription/tier management CRUD, token rate limiting enforcement, API key lifecycle, OIDC user authentication.\n- Exercise the deployment-related failure modes from the strategy: Limitador pod termination (HTTP 503 denial), cert-manager TLS certificate rotation without connection errors.\n- Document what works, what breaks, and the engineering delta (code changes, configuration changes, Helm chart packaging gaps), plus the known-limitations list.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a CKS cluster with RHCL/Kuadrant and Gateway API (Istio) installed, when MaaS is deployed via Helm chart with OIDC configuration, then the maas-api and maas-controller pods are running and healthy, measured by pod readiness checks passing.\n- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with OIDC configured, when a user authenticates with a valid OIDC JWT token and creates an API key, then the API key is persisted in PostgreSQL and can be used for model inference, measured by a successful inference request using the generated API key.\n- Given a MaaSSubscription with token rate limits configured, when a user exceeds the rate limit, then Limitador returns HTTP 429, measured by monitoring the response status codes.\n- Given a MaaS deployment with Limitador pod terminated, when a user makes an inference request, then the request is denied with HTTP 503, measured by response status and Envoy logs showing upstream connection failure.\n- Given cert-manager-issued TLS certificates, when the certificates are rotated, then active inference requests continue without interruption and new requests succeed with the new certificate, measured by zero connection errors during the rotation window and successful TLS handshake validation post-rotation.\n- Kuadrant is deployed via the mechanism selected by the investigation, measured by Authorino enforcing the MaaS AuthPolicy on the CKS gateway.\n- A document exists listing all known limitations of MaaS on xKS versus RHOAI MaaS GA, including the engineering delta (what works, what breaks, changes needed).\n- The MaaS 3.4 build used as baseline is identified (GA or RC per the baseline feasibility investigation).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] MaaS successfully deployed on CKS (priority platform per Staff Engineer Input)\n- [P0] Token rate limiting functional on xKS\n- [P0] External OIDC authentication validated for user identity (validation)\n- [P0] API key authentication (sk-oai-* flow) functional on xKS (validation)\n- [P1] Tier/subscription management functional with OIDC group claims (validation)\n- [P1] Known limitations documented\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":61263,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab07d7148cbf06fc","agent_id":"a5dd9ebccf03d402c","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4feb-9959-cd45ee4b4e7a","uuid":"9f7a0058-d491-4b23-a346-66abb6ee99d6","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:56:39.587Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003"}
