l inference request using the generated API key.\n- Given a MaaSSubscription with token rate limits configured on AKS, when a user exceeds the rate limit, then HTTP 429 is returned, measured by monitoring response status codes.\n- AKS-specific known limitations are appended to the known-limitations document produced by the CKS validation.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] MaaS successfully deployed on AKS (RFE acceptance criterion: \"AKS AND CKS\")\n- [P0] Token rate limiting functional on xKS (AKS confirmation)\n- [P0] External OIDC authentication validated for user identity (AKS confirmation)\n- [P0] API key authentication (sk-oai-* flow) functional on xKS (AKS confirmation)\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":61263,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab07d7148cbf06fc","agent_id":"a5dd9ebccf03d402c","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4feb-9959-cd45ee4b4e7a","uuid":"741ace1d-bbc6-4f64-9b53-57b3fbd77966","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:56:50.586Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003"}
