{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-57cff890-1460-4d0b-85d6-fb652d34b03b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6358123c47e4a65","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-oimz6d8o/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-BRANCH-C-E012.md","content":"# Contingency: Direct Envoy ext_authz Authentication and Rate Limiting for MaaS on xKS\n\n## Description\n\nContingency implementation activated only if the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS deployment path investigation resolves to outcome C — Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) cannot be deployed on xKS. Replaces the Authorino-based authentication enforcement with direct Envoy ext_authz integration for MaaS authentication and rate limiting, preserving the external OIDC authentication and API key validation capabilities required by the strategy.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Wire Envoy ext_authz at the MaaS gateway to perform bearer-token authentication (external OIDC JWT validation and API key validation via the maas-api callback endpoint) in place of Kuadrant/Authorino AuthPolicy enforcement.\n- Provide token rate limiting equivalent to the Limitador-backed TokenRateLimitPolicy behavior (HTTP 429 on exceeded quota), using an Envoy-compatible rate limiting mechanism.\n- Integrate with the Helm-based MaaS xKS installation so the contingency path is selectable via chart configuration.\n- Preserve the strategy's failure-mode behavior: API key requests continue to succeed during IdP unavailability (OIDC-authenticated requests fail with HTTP 503); rate limiting enforcement unavailability denies requests with HTTP 503.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given an xKS cluster where Kuadrant cannot be installed, when MaaS is deployed with the Envoy ext_authz authentication configuration, then OIDC JWT authentication and API key (`sk-oai-*`) authentication both succeed, measured by successful authenticated inference requests.\n- Given token rate limits configured, when a user exceeds the rate limit, then HTTP 429 is returned, measured by monitoring response status codes.\n- Given the authentication service becomes unavailable, when a user makes an inference request, then the request is denied with HTTP 503, measured by response status and Envoy logs showing upstream connection failure.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] External OIDC authentication validated for user identity (contingency path)\n- [P0] API key authentication (sk-oai-* flow) functional on xKS (contingency path)\n- [P0] Token rate limiting functional on xKS (contingency path)\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":68735,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab07d7148cbf06fc","agent_id":"a5dd9ebccf03d402c","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4feb-9959-cd45ee4b4e7a","uuid":"e0869317-a7f9-4baa-bb01-096b4c554cea","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:58:00.102Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8003"}
