{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a548da27e3a2df3d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n3\ttitle: RHCL/Kuadrant xKS deployment path investigation\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Inference Gateway\n6\tteam: RHCL / OpenShift\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -2\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -3\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# RHCL/Kuadrant xKS Deployment Path Investigation\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves the strategy's strategic dependency on RHCL (Red Hat Common Libraries) support for non-OpenShift Kubernetes: whether Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) can be officially deployed and supported on xKS, by which mechanism, and whether it functions on CKS with the Istio GatewayClass. The outcome selects the deployment approach used by all downstream xKS validation and authentication work.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Engage the OpenShift RHCL team to confirm official xKS (Helm-based) support commitment and timeline; escalate to product leadership if not committed (per the strategy's Sprint 1 validation directive).\n34\t- Determine whether official RHCL/Kuadrant Helm charts exist (or are planned) for CKS.\n35\t- Validate that Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) installs and functions on a CKS test cluster with the Istio GatewayClass, including basic AuthPolicy and TokenRateLimitPolicy reconciliation.\n36\t- Produce a decision record selecting one of the strategy's three bounded deployment options:\n37\t  - **Outcome A**: RHCL Helm charts (primary — requires OpenShift team commitment)\n38\t  - **Outcome B**: standalone Authorino + Limitador via Helm (fallback)\n39\t  - **Outcome C**: direct Envoy ext_authz integration (contingency — triggers the branched contingency epic)\n40\t\n41\t## Acceptance Criteria\n42\t\n43\t- A written decision record exists stating the RHCL official xKS support status (committed / not committed, with timeline) and the selected Kuadrant deployment mechanism for xKS.\n44\t- If outcome A or B: Kuadrant is installed on a CKS test cluster and Authorino enforces a test AuthPolicy while Limitador enforces a test token rate limit, measured by successful policy reconciliation and a rate-limited request returning HTTP 429.\n45\t- If outcome C: the decision record documents the specific CKS blockers that rule out Kuadrant, and the contingency branch is activated.\n46\t\n47\t## HLR Traceability\n48\t\n49\t- [P0] RHCL official xKS support status confirmed and deployment mechanism validated (per Staff Engineer Input)\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9bff3f11e550c700","agent_id":"a83f285f4e7cc5ad9","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4feb-9959-cd45ee4b4e7a","uuid":"95a293e9-b397-4e75-b461-276d18318e95","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:01:50.111Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a548da27e3a2df3d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
