{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f81ecf0df25d048","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E009\n3\ttitle: MaaS observability integration on xKS (dashboards, Prometheus, Loki)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model and Agent Observability\n6\tteam: xKS Platform\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E006\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E007\n13\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If CKS Prometheus/Loki are not accessible for MaaS, self-provision\n17\t    the observability infrastructure for the Dev Preview per the validation report's\n18\t    recommendation.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 0\n24\t  open_questions: 0\n25\t  external_dependency: -1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 0\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Medium\n32\tai_implementability_score: 1\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# MaaS Observability Integration on xKS: Dashboards, Prometheus, and Loki\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tIntegrates MaaS observability signals with the CKS observability stack: deploys Perses dashboards for MaaS metrics, wires the CKS Prometheus instance to scrape MaaS metrics endpoints, and integrates structured logs (maas-api, Authorino, Limitador) with CKS Grafana Loki. Owned by the xKS Platform team with MaaS and RHCL involvement; depends on the CKS observability infrastructure validation confirming accessibility.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Perses dashboards for MaaS displaying token usage per subscription, rate limiting enforcement events, and API key lifecycle metrics over the last 24 hours.\n45\t- Integration with the xKS/CKS Prometheus instance so MaaS metrics endpoints are scraped (per the validation outcome: scrape target configuration and access).\n46\t- Integration of structured logs with CKS Grafana Loki, including the structured logging configuration for Authorino (authentication decisions) and Limitador (rate limit enforcement) with RHCL configuration guidance, and maas-api API key validation events.\n47\t- Log label filters supporting the strategy's logging acceptance criteria (identity, method, decision, reason).\n48\t- If the CKS infrastructure validation found Prometheus or Loki inaccessible, implement the recommended fallback (e.g., self-provisioned instances for the Dev Preview).\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with Prometheus integration, when a user creates an API key, makes inference requests, and exceeds a rate limit, then Prometheus metrics include `maas_api_key_created_total`, `maas_inference_requests_total{user, model, subscription}`, and `maas_rate_limit_enforced_total{user, model, exceeded_quota}`, measured by querying the CKS Prometheus instance.\n53\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with structured logging enabled, when an authentication event occurs (success or failure), then the log entry includes timestamp, user identity, authentication method (OIDC/API key), decision (allow/deny), and reason (if denied), measured by querying CKS Grafana Loki with label filters.\n54\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with Perses dashboards installed, when an admin navigates to the MaaS observability dashboard, then the dashboard displays token usage per subscription, rate limiting enforcement events, and API key lifecycle metrics over the last 24 hours, measured by dashboard rendering with live data.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- [P0] Observability metrics functional: token usage, rate limiting enforcement, API key lifecycle events (per Staff Engineer Input) — integration side\n59\t- [P1] Observability logging functional: authentication events, rate limit enforcement, subscription selection (per Staff Engineer Input) — integration side\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9bff3f11e550c700","agent_id":"a83f285f4e7cc5ad9","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4feb-9959-cd45ee4b4e7a","uuid":"ca1fa5b2-17b7-48f5-b56e-b0f9b4fcef1e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:02:09.642Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f81ecf0df25d048","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
