{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f62a6fe5d049cec","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E006\n3\ttitle: MaaS observability instrumentation (metrics and structured logging)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E003\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E003\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If maas-api instrumentation is not feasible without MaaS 3.4\n15\t    GA code changes, deliver metrics as a post-3.4 patch or defer the P1 logging scope\n16\t    per the strategy risk table.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 4\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# MaaS Observability Instrumentation: Metrics and Structured Logging\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tInstruments maas-api (and related MaaS components where needed) with the observability signals the strategy designates as a core value proposition for MaaS on xKS: Prometheus metrics for token usage, rate limiting enforcement, API key lifecycle, and inference latency (P0), plus structured JSON logging for API key validation and authentication-related events in maas-api (P1, bundled because it touches the same code paths).\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Prometheus metrics instrumentation in maas-api, exposed on the `/metrics` endpoint (an internal metrics route already exists per architecture context: models-as-a-service.md):\n43\t  - API key lifecycle events (creation, validation, revocation), e.g. `maas_api_key_created_total`\n44\t  - Token usage and inference requests per user/model/subscription, e.g. `maas_inference_requests_total{user, model, subscription}`\n45\t  - Rate limiting enforcement, e.g. `maas_rate_limit_enforced_total{user, model, exceeded_quota}`\n46\t  - Inference request latency\n47\t- Structured JSON logging in maas-api for API key validation and authentication-relevant events, including timestamp, user identity, authentication method, decision, and reason.\n48\t- Async metric emission to bound observability overhead; if p99 overhead exceeds 5 ms, move emission to post-response goroutines (per the strategy's risk mitigation).\n49\t- If maas-api instrumentation is not feasible without MaaS 3.4 GA code changes (resolved by the baseline feasibility investigation), deliver it as a post-3.4 patch or defer the P1 logging scope, per the strategy's risk table.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with Prometheus integration, when a user creates an API key, makes inference requests, and exceeds a rate limit, then Prometheus metrics include API key creation, inference request, and rate limit enforcement counters with the labels above, measured by querying the CKS Prometheus instance.\n54\t- Inference request latency metrics are exposed and queryable, measured by Prometheus query.\n55\t- Given structured logging enabled, when an API key validation event occurs (success or failure), then the log entry includes timestamp, user identity, authentication method, decision, and reason, measured by log inspection with label filters.\n56\t- Observability overhead does not exceed the strategy's p99 5 ms threshold, measured by latency benchmarking; if exceeded, emission is moved to post-response processing.\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability\n59\t\n60\t- [P0] Observability metrics functional: token usage, rate limiting enforcement, API key lifecycle events (per Staff Engineer Input)\n61\t- [P1] Observability logging functional: authentication events, rate limit enforcement, subscription selection (per Staff Engineer Input) — maas-api side\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9dff2f9036b28837","agent_id":"a9d6226c814588f52","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4feb-9959-cd45ee4b4e7a","uuid":"09fedab3-b9b4-4b6d-ad21-c1a618ae9b1a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:12:04.200Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f62a6fe5d049cec","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
