h configuration for non-standard claim formats (e.g., Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`) and its effect on tier mapping\n49\t- Consolidated known-limitations topic drawing on the documented limitations and engineering delta from the CKS and AKS validation work.\n50\t- Content outline validated for technical accuracy against the implemented behavior and the architecture context (models-as-a-service.md).\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- A published documentation topic exists describing the user identity flow for xKS deployments, covering OIDC provider configuration, token flow, API key lifecycle, and group claim mapping.\n55\t- A known-limitations topic exists consolidating the CKS and AKS validation findings for MaaS on xKS versus RHOAI MaaS GA.\n56\t- Documentation is technically reviewed against the actual implementation (behavior verified on a deployed xKS MaaS instance) before publication.\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability\n59\t\n60\t- [P2] User identity flow documented for xKS deployments\n61\t- [P1] Known limitations documented (consolidation of validation deliverables)\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9dff2f9036b28837","agent_id":"a9d6226c814588f52","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4feb-9959-cd45ee4b4e7a","uuid":"0c3bdcb8-a3ec-44c4-be0b-cf2737d6d28e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:12:24.132Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac72fb7c396051de","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
