{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-832a7a5d-b2cd-42e3-8040-13f32ac48175","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The review prompt says: \"For every epic that lists an Investigation in `dependencies`, verify `gated_by` is set — an Investigation dependency without `gated_by` is a major issue.\" And \"Verify that every `gated_by` target appears in that epic's direct `dependencies` list.\"\n\nSince `gated_by` is a single string in the schema, and E005/E007 depend on two Investigations (E001 and E003), both of which are true gates... The review says \"set `gated_by` (or split gates)\". Since the schema is a single string, the cleanest schema-compliant representation for multiple gates... Hmm. Maybe frontmatter.py supports a list for gated_by? The schema says type: string. Let me check frontmatter.py to see if it can set a list value and whether validation would reject a list for gated_by. If a list would fail validation, use a comma-separated string? But then \"gated_by target appears in dependencies\" check — automated consumers parse gated_by as a single epic_id.\n\nAlternative reading: \"or split gates\" — i.e., keep gated_by as the strongest/primary gate? No, the review says \"the gate must be reflected in gated_by\" for E003.\n\nLet me look at scripts/frontmatter.py to see how set handles values and validation.","signature":"a82902bd493d4af4bf65a46fd1a325b7"}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":43896,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9dff2f9036b28837","agent_id":"a9d6226c814588f52","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4feb-9959-cd45ee4b4e7a","uuid":"48c65610-34f1-4a8f-8bf1-8c5942d32f61","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:14:23.855Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
