{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-fcb2191a-af26-49df-9e8e-6566e56a2970","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba4aeb8c01b00430","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-oimz6d8o/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8003-E013.md","content":"# Structured Logging Instrumentation in maas-api\n\n## Description\n\nAdds the P1 structured-logging deliverable for MaaS on xKS: structured JSON logs in maas-api for API key validation, authentication-relevant events, and subscription selection decisions, formatted for aggregation in CKS Grafana Loki. Split from the P0 metrics instrumentation so the P1 logging scope can be deferred independently per the strategy's risk table, without affecting the P0 observability deliverable.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Structured JSON logging in maas-api for API key validation and authentication-relevant events, including timestamp, user identity, authentication method (OIDC/API key), decision (allow/deny), and reason (if denied).\n- Structured log entries for subscription/tier selection decisions (which subscription was selected for a request and the triggering identity), per the strategy's logging requirement.\n- Log fields and labels formatted for aggregation in CKS Grafana Loki (label filters on identity, method, decision, reason per the strategy's logging acceptance criteria); the log-shipping/integration side is handled by the logging integration deliverable on xKS.\n- If maas-api is frozen in the MaaS 3.4 GA baseline (resolved by the baseline feasibility investigation), deliver structured logging as a post-3.4 patch or defer this P1 scope per the strategy's risk table.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given structured logging enabled in maas-api, when an API key validation event occurs (success or failure), then the log entry is emitted as structured JSON including timestamp, user identity, authentication method, decision, and reason, measured by log inspection with label filters.\n- Given structured logging enabled, when a subscription selection decision occurs, then the log entry records the selected subscription/tier and the triggering user identity, measured by log inspection.\n- Log emission stays within the strategy's observability overhead budget (p99 5 ms threshold, async/post-response emission if exceeded), measured by latency benchmarking.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P1] Observability logging functional: authentication events, rate limit enforcement, subscription selection (per Staff Engineer Input) — maas-api instrumentation side\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":57620,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9dff2f9036b28837","agent_id":"a9d6226c814588f52","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4feb-9959-cd45ee4b4e7a","uuid":"1fb36731-a970-4f62-955e-b592d82877f6","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:18:41.051Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
