{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9af22e30886f7020","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E006\n3\ttitle: MaaS observability metrics instrumentation\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E003\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E003\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If maas-api instrumentation is not feasible without MaaS 3.4\n15\t    GA code changes, deliver the metrics as a post-3.4 patch per the strategy risk\n16\t    table; the P1 structured-logging scope is planned as a separately deferrable epic\n17\t    and is not affected by this gate.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 4\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# MaaS Observability Metrics Instrumentation\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tInstruments maas-api (and related MaaS components where needed) with the P0 observability signal the strategy designates as a core value proposition for MaaS on xKS: Prometheus metrics for token usage, rate limiting enforcement, API key lifecycle, and inference latency. The P1 structured-logging scope is planned as a separate, independently deferrable epic so it can be dropped without affecting the P0 metrics deliverable.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Prometheus metrics instrumentation in maas-api, exposed on the `/metrics` endpoint (an internal metrics route already exists per architecture context: models-as-a-service.md):\n44\t  - API key lifecycle events (creation, validation, revocation), e.g. `maas_api_key_created_total`\n45\t  - Token usage and inference requests per user/model/subscription, e.g. `maas_inference_requests_total{user, model, subscription}`\n46\t  - Rate limiting enforcement, e.g. `maas_rate_limit_enforced_total{user, model, exceeded_quota}`\n47\t  - Inference request latency\n48\t- Async metric emission to bound observability overhead; if p99 overhead exceeds 5 ms, move emission to post-response goroutines (per the strategy's risk mitigation).\n49\t- If maas-api instrumentation is not feasible without MaaS 3.4 GA code changes (resolved by the baseline feasibility investigation), deliver the metrics as a post-3.4 patch per the strategy's risk table; the P1 structured-logging scope is planned separately and can be deferred independently.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with Prometheus integration, when a user creates an API key, makes inference requests, and exceeds a rate limit, then Prometheus metrics include API key creation, inference request, and rate limit enforcement counters with the labels above, measured by querying the CKS Prometheus instance.\n54\t- Inference request latency metrics are exposed and queryable, measured by Prometheus query.\n55\t- Observability overhead does not exceed the strategy's p99 5 ms threshold, measured by latency benchmarking; if exceeded, emission is moved to post-response processing.\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\t- [P0] Observability metrics functional: token usage, rate limiting enforcement, API key lifecycle events (per Staff Engineer Input)\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bed058a549fc6594","agent_id":"a1af9d088ca09e8e3","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4feb-9959-cd45ee4b4e7a","uuid":"dfda0b33-5729-435a-aa84-74ac98857121","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:23:00.592Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9af22e30886f7020","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
