{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b4a715e44c6dbef","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E008\n3\ttitle: MaaS deployment validation on AKS\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E007\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: Same Kuadrant contingency as the CKS validation; AKS uses a different\n16\t    Gateway API implementation (envoy-gateway or azure-application-gateway), so gateway-class\n17\t    findings from CKS may require adaptation.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: -1\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 3\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# MaaS Deployment Validation on AKS\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tExtends the validated MaaS xKS deployment to Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS), satisfying the RFE acceptance criterion \"AKS AND CKS\". Builds on the CKS validation's engineering delta and findings; AKS uses a different Gateway API implementation than CKS's Istio (validated options per the strategy: `envoy-gateway` multi-platform or `azure-application-gateway`).\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Deploy MaaS on an AKS cluster via the Helm-based installation, using a GatewayClass supported on AKS (envoy-gateway or azure-application-gateway per the strategy's validated options).\n44\t- Deploy Kuadrant (Authorino + Limitador) via the mechanism selected by the RHCL/Kuadrant xKS deployment path investigation, confirming it on AKS as well.\n45\t- Configure an external OIDC identity provider and exercise user authentication.\n46\t- Validate the same core functionality validated on CKS: subscription/tier management, token rate limiting, API key lifecycle, OIDC authentication, and pod readiness.\n47\t- Apply the engineering delta discovered during the CKS validation; document any AKS-specific gaps or limitations.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Given an AKS cluster with RHCL/Kuadrant and Gateway API installed, when MaaS is deployed via Helm chart with OIDC configuration, then the maas-api and maas-controller pods are running and healthy, measured by pod readiness checks passing.\n52\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on AKS with OIDC configured, when a user authenticates with a valid OIDC JWT token and creates an API key, then the API key is persisted and usable for inference, measured by a successful inference request using the generated API key.\n53\t- Given a MaaSSubscription with token rate limits configured on AKS, when a user exceeds the rate limit, then HTTP 429 is returned, measured by monitoring response status codes.\n54\t- AKS-specific known limitations are appended to the known-limitations document produced by the CKS validation.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- [P0] MaaS successfully deployed on AKS (RFE acceptance criterion: \"AKS AND CKS\")\n59\t- [P0] Token rate limiting functional on xKS (AKS confirmation)\n60\t- [P0] External OIDC authentication validated for user identity (AKS confirmation)\n61\t- [P0] API key authentication (sk-oai-* flow) functional on xKS (AKS confirmation)\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bed058a549fc6594","agent_id":"a1af9d088ca09e8e3","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4feb-9959-cd45ee4b4e7a","uuid":"9f8a2c6d-84a9-452d-828d-0a6c706ebaa1","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:23:06.229Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b4a715e44c6dbef","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_