{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88aab5ce9dd72ad0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E009\n3\ttitle: MaaS observability integration on xKS (dashboards, Prometheus)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model and Agent Observability\n6\tteam: xKS Platform\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E006\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E007\n13\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the CKS Prometheus instance is not accessible for MaaS metrics,\n17\t    self-provision the metrics collection for the Dev Preview per the validation report\n18\t    recommendation.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 0\n24\t  open_questions: 0\n25\t  external_dependency: -1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 0\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Medium\n32\tai_implementability_score: 1\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# MaaS Observability Integration on xKS: Dashboards and Prometheus\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tIntegrates the MaaS P0 observability signals with the CKS observability stack: deploys Perses dashboards for MaaS metrics and wires the CKS Prometheus instance to scrape MaaS metrics endpoints. The P1 structured-logging integration with CKS Grafana Loki is planned as a separate, independently deferrable epic. Owned by the xKS Platform team with MaaS involvement; depends on the CKS observability infrastructure validation confirming accessibility.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Perses dashboards for MaaS displaying token usage per subscription, rate limiting enforcement events, and API key lifecycle metrics over the last 24 hours.\n45\t- Integration with the xKS/CKS Prometheus instance so MaaS metrics endpoints are scraped (per the validation outcome: scrape target configuration and access).\n46\t- If the CKS infrastructure validation found Prometheus inaccessible, implement the recommended fallback (e.g., a self-provisioned instance for the Dev Preview).\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with Prometheus integration, when a user creates an API key, makes inference requests, and exceeds a rate limit, then Prometheus metrics include `maas_api_key_created_total`, `maas_inference_requests_total{user, model, subscription}`, and `maas_rate_limit_enforced_total{user, model, exceeded_quota}`, measured by querying the CKS Prometheus instance.\n51\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with Perses dashboards installed, when an admin navigates to the MaaS observability dashboard, then the dashboard displays token usage per subscription, rate limiting enforcement events, and API key lifecycle metrics over the last 24 hours, measured by dashboard rendering with live data.\n52\t\n53\t## HLR Traceability\n54\t\n55\t- [P0] Observability metrics functional: token usage, rate limiting enforcement, API key lifecycle events (per Staff Engineer Input) — integration side\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bed058a549fc6594","agent_id":"a1af9d088ca09e8e3","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4feb-9959-cd45ee4b4e7a","uuid":"0b6a268f-5b98-4ea9-8070-cc27e6409a67","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:23:07.422Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-88aab5ce9dd72ad0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
