{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bca48793c0ada9b9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E014\n3\ttitle: Structured logging integration on xKS (Loki, Authorino/Limitador logging configuration)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model and Agent Observability\n6\tteam: xKS Platform / RHCL / OpenShift\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E007\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E013\n13\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If CKS Grafana Loki is not accessible for MaaS logs, self-provision\n17\t    the log aggregation for the Dev Preview per the validation report recommendation.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 0\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: -1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 0\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Medium\n31\tai_implementability_score: 1\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Structured Logging Integration on xKS: Grafana Loki, Authorino, and Limitador\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tIntegrates the MaaS P1 structured-logging deliverable with the CKS log-aggregation stack: ships maas-api structured logs to CKS Grafana Loki and configures structured logging for Authorino (authentication decisions) and Limitador (rate limit enforcement). The Authorino/Limitador logging configuration is work the strategy's Affected Components table assigns to RHCL/OpenShift (external) — this epic is explicitly co-owned by the xKS Platform team and RHCL/OpenShift, with RHCL providing the logging configuration for their components and xKS Platform owning the Loki integration. Split from the P0 metrics integration so the P1 logging scope can be deferred independently.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Integration of maas-api structured logs with CKS Grafana Loki, building on the log format and labels emitted by the structured-logging instrumentation deliverable (identity, method, decision, reason).\n44\t- Structured logging configuration for Authorino (authentication decisions) and Limitador (rate limit enforcement) — co-owned with RHCL/OpenShift per the strategy's Affected Components and Impacted Teams tables: RHCL owns the logging configuration for these components, with the configuration guidance captured and applied on the xKS side.\n45\t- Log label filters and Loki queries supporting the strategy's logging acceptance criteria (timestamp, user identity, authentication method, decision, reason).\n46\t- A running MaaS instance on CKS (from the CKS deployment validation) to collect logs from.\n47\t- If the CKS infrastructure validation found Loki inaccessible for MaaS, implement the recommended fallback (e.g., a self-provisioned log-aggregation instance for the Dev Preview).\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with structured logging enabled, when an authentication event occurs (success or failure) in maas-api, then the log entry is aggregated in CKS Grafana Loki and retrievable with label filters on timestamp, user identity, authentication method (OIDC/API key), decision (allow/deny), and reason (if denied), measured by querying CKS Grafana Loki.\n52\t- Given the Authorino and Limitador structured-logging configuration co-owned with RHCL/OpenShift, when an authentication decision or rate limit enforcement event occurs, then the corresponding structured log entry reaches CKS Grafana Loki, measured by Loki queries for those components' logs.\n53\t- Given a MaaSSubscription with token rate limits configured, when a user exceeds the rate limit, then the rate limit enforcement event (429 with exceeded quota) is retrievable from Loki, measured by Loki query.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- [P1] Observability logging functional: authentication events, rate limit enforcement, subscription selection (per Staff Engineer Input) — integration side (Loki, Authorino/Limitador logging configuration)\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bed058a549fc6594","agent_id":"a1af9d088ca09e8e3","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4feb-9959-cd45ee4b4e7a","uuid":"8612e4c4-9d6a-43f3-adf2-62aa2991f049","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:23:16.265Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bca48793c0ada9b9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8003 decomposition"}
