ed AC gaps found (BRANCH-C-E012 is a contingency path, not a replacement of an existing production capability). No draft-ID references to sibling epics appear in any epic body.\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n\nThe epic set accounts for the full strategy scope: user management strategy (E005), Helm packaging (E004), CKS and AKS validation (E007/E008, satisfying the \"AKS AND CKS\" RFE criterion), RHCL strategic dependency with all three bounded outcomes (E001 + BRANCH-C-E012 for outcome C, A/B absorbed as an AC on the validation epics), observability metrics/logging/tracing (E006/E009, E013/E014, E010), documentation (E011). All strategy acceptance criteria — happy path and failure modes (OIDC outage, Limitador termination, cert rotation, PostgreSQL unavailability) — map to epic ACs. Strategy-level context is carried forward rather than dropped: risk mitigations appear as conditional scope (LRU cache on E005, p99 5 ms on E006/E013, escalation path in E001's gate), and the open questions are distributed to the right epics (OIDC caching → E005, shared/dedicated PostgreSQL → E004 AC, stable build date → E003, RHCL charts → E001, CKS Prometheus/Loki → E002). The xKS-Platform installer integration mentioned only in the Impacted Teams table is transparently flagged as a potential follow-up (Health Warning #6) rather than silently dropped or invented — correct handling of out-of-HLR scope. Documentation Support is \"Pending human review\" (not \"Yes\") and a docs-authoring epic exists regardless. Minor observation, not scored: the strategy is internally inconsistent on tracing priority (NFR says P1, HLR list and Technical Approach say P2); the decomposition followed the HLR list, which is the defensible choice.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":74712,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bed058a549fc6594","agent_id":"a1af9d088ca09e8e3","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4f