t/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/ai-gateway-operator.md:24:A notable architectural characteristic is the operator's role as an integration hub: it manages Kuadrant AuthPolicies and TokenRateLimitPolicies for API authentication and rate limiting, Istio networking resources (DestinationRules, EnvoyFilters, ServiceEntries) for service mesh integration, Gateway API HTTPRoutes for traffic routing, cert-manager Certificates for TLS, and OpenTelemetry collectors and Perses dashboards for observability. This positions the operator as the single control point for the MaaS (Model-as-a-Service) infrastructure stack, creating a wide RBAC footprint (57 rules in the manager role) that spans multiple API groups.\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-oimz6d8o/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/ai-gateway-operator.md:181:| ai-gateway-manager-role | opentelemetry.io | opentelemetrycollectors | create, delete, get, list, patch, watch |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-oimz6d8o/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/ai-gateway-operator.md:250:| manager-role | opentelemetry.io | opentelemetrycollectors | create, delete, get, list, patch, watch |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-oimz6d8o/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/ai-gateway-operator.md:316:- **Resource creation chain:** During reconciliation, the operator renders kustomize manifests from `/manifests/` and creates/updates downstream resources across multiple API groups: Gateway API resources (HTTPRoutes, Gateways), Kuadrant policies (AuthPolicies, TokenRateLimitPolicies, RateLimitPolicies), Istio networking (DestinationRules, EnvoyFilters, ServiceEntries), cert-manager Certificates, Deployments, RBAC objects, NetworkPolicies, and observability resources (ServiceMonitors, OpenTelemetry collectors, Perses dashboards). [source: config/rbac/role.yaml:2, internal/controller/aigateway/aigateway_controller.go:155-166]\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-oimz6d8o/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/odh-observability.md:14:**Short**: odh-observability is a Kubernetes operator that deploys and manages a unified observability stack—Prometheus monitoring, distributed tracing via Tempo, and usage log collection via LokiStack—for the RHOAI platform through a singleton cluster-scoped `Monitoring` custom resource. [source: api/v1alpha1/monitoring_types.go:39-66, cmd/main.go:61-155, charts/odh-observability/crds/services.platform.opendatahub.io_monitorings.yaml:2]\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-oimz6d8o/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/odh-observability.md:16:**Detailed**: odh-observability implements a controller-runtime operator that reconciles a cluster-scoped `Monitoring` custom resource (`services.platform.opendatahub.io/v1alpha1`) to deploy and configure a complete observability stack for RHOAI. The operator manages Prometheus-based metrics collection with configurable storage and retention, distributed tracing through the Tempo operator with S3/GCS/PV storage backends, and usage log collection via LokiStack with OpenTelemetry collectors. It deploys kube-rbac-proxy sidecars for authenticated Prometheus access through SubjectAccessReview-based authorization and creates OpenShift Routes for external TLS exposure. The operator uses odh-platform-utilities for server-side-apply deployment via the `deploy.Deployer`, platform detection, and shared API types including the `PlatformObject` interface for standardized status and condition management across RHOAI services. A mutating admission webhook injects monitoring labels into PodMonitor and ServiceMonitor resources to ensure consistent metrics collection across data science workloads. [source: api/v1alpha1/monitoring_types.go:20-41, cmd/main.go:40-134, internal/controller/resources/data-science-prometheus-cluster-proxy.tmpl.yaml:58-93, Dockerfiles/Dockerfile.konflux:19]\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-oimz6d8o/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/odh-observability.md:22:The architecture has three functional tiers. The operator itself runs as a single manager process exposing health probes on port 8081 and an optional webhook on port 9443. The data plane consists of controller-managed Prometheus instances, kube-rbac-proxy sidecars for both cluster-scoped and namespace-scoped proxy access, prom-label-proxy for namespace-scoped metric filtering, and OpenTelemetry collectors for metrics processing and usage log forwarding to LokiStack. External access is provided through three OpenShift Routes—two for Prometheus proxy endpoints and one for Thanos Querier—all using TLS. [source: cmd/main.go:70-74, 86-101, internal/controller/resources/data-science-prometheus-cluster-proxy.tmpl.yaml:58-97]\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-oimz6d8o/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/odh-observability.md:245:The MonitoringReconciler watches the `Monitoring` CR and a broad set of dependent resources (Deployments, Secrets, ConfigMaps, Services, Routes, RBAC, NetworkPolicies, CRDs, Jobs). On each reconciliation, it renders Go templates into Kubernetes manifests and applies them via server-side apply through odh-platform-utilities' Deployer. The reconciler manages the full observability stack lifecycle including Prometheus instances, proxy deployments, OpenTelemetry collectors, and webhook infrastructure. [source: cmd/main.go:109-128, internal/controller/actions.go:580-614]\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8003-oimz6d8o/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/kserve.md:224:| github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-