{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87a30d076f38fcbb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E004\n3\ttitle: MaaS Helm chart packaging for xKS\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# MaaS Helm Chart Packaging for xKS\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tPackages the MaaS components (maas-api, maas-controller, payload-processing BBR ext_proc server) as Helm charts for deployment on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (xKS), replacing the OLM-based operator installation used on RHOAI. This is the foundational packaging work that all xKS deployment validation builds against.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Helm charts for maas-api, maas-controller, and the payload-processing ext_proc server, built from the existing deployment manifests (architecture context: models-as-a-service.md, deployment/base).\n38\t- Configurable chart values for:\n39\t  - Gateway class name (Istio `GatewayClass` for CKS as priority platform; other validated options such as `envoy-gateway` for multi-platform and `azure-application-gateway` for AKS)\n40\t  - OIDC issuer configuration (issuer URL, client ID, audience, group claim path) for tenants that configure external OIDC\n41\t  - TLS certificate source via cert-manager (replacing OpenShift service-CA auto-generated certificates)\n42\t  - PostgreSQL connection, supporting either a shared (with other RHAII components) or dedicated instance\n43\t  - Group claim path mapping value\n44\t- Remove OpenShift-specific installation assumptions (no OLM; no `openshift-default` GatewayClass requirement) while keeping RHOAI deployments unaffected (additive/configuration-driven per the strategy's backwards-compatibility NFR).\n45\t- The existing Gateway API HTTPRoutes are GatewayClass-agnostic per architecture context, so routing manifests carry over with configurable gateway/parent references.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- Given a non-OpenShift Kubernetes cluster with a supported Gateway API implementation installed, when the MaaS Helm chart is installed with values set for that platform's gateway class, then maas-api, maas-controller, and payload-processing pods are running and healthy, measured by pod readiness checks passing.\n50\t- TLS certificates are issued via cert-manager and served on the MaaS API endpoints, measured by successful TLS handshake validation.\n51\t- The PostgreSQL connection is configurable for both shared and dedicated instances, measured by successful chart installation against each mode (resolves the shared-vs-dedicated open question as a configuration value, not a code change).\n52\t- Chart values expose the OIDC issuer and group claim path configuration surface used by the external OIDC authentication capability.\n53\t- Build pipeline for the Helm chart artifacts is green (the strategy's build onboarding prerequisite is satisfied for the chart).\n54\t- RHOAI MaaS GA deployments are unchanged by this work (no regression to the OLM-based path).\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- [P0] MaaS successfully deployed on CKS (packaging prerequisite)\n59\t- [P0] MaaS successfully deployed on AKS (packaging prerequisite)\n60\t- Out-of-scope confirmation: operator-based installation on xKS is excluded (Helm only per RFE)\n61\t\n62\t## Risks\n63\t\n64\t- Helm chart build pipeline onboarding is a pending human-review prerequisite in the strategy; if the review requires dedicated pipeline work, a follow-up epic may be needed.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a96c07aedf57c588","agent_id":"a43da7aa6bd0b6b38","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4feb-9959-cd45ee4b4e7a","uuid":"763f2ba0-26d5-4156-b0dd-a928f6be09d6","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:39:58.009Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-87a30d076f38fcbb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Second revise RHAISTRAT-8003"}
