ce from OIDC/IdP availability\n50\t  - Group claim path configuration for non-standard claim formats (e.g., Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`) and its effect on tier mapping\n51\t- Consolidated known-limitations topic drawing on the documented limitations and engineering delta from the CKS and AKS validation work.\n52\t- Content outline validated for technical accuracy against the implemented behavior and the architecture context (models-as-a-service.md).\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- A published documentation topic exists describing the user identity flow for xKS deployments, covering OIDC provider configuration, token flow, API key lifecycle, and group claim mapping.\n57\t- A known-limitations topic exists consolidating the CKS and AKS validation findings for MaaS on xKS versus RHOAI MaaS GA.\n58\t- Documentation is technically reviewed against the actual implementation (behavior verified on a deployed xKS MaaS instance) before publication.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- [P2] User identity flow documented for xKS deployments\n63\t- [P1] Known limitations documented (consolidation of validation deliverables)\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a96c07aedf57c588","agent_id":"a43da7aa6bd0b6b38","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4feb-9959-cd45ee4b4e7a","uuid":"112f0e85-9521-4a87-83fd-3576e68ccd57","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:39:58.883Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a82c2db750e9ea59","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Second revise RHAISTRAT-8003"}
