 strategy's Affected Components and Impacted Teams tables: RHCL owns the logging configuration for these components, with the configuration guidance captured and applied on the xKS side.\n- Structured logging configuration for Limitador covering rate limit enforcement events (429 with exceeded quota).\n- Shipping the Authorino and Limitador structured logs into the log-aggregation deliverable (CKS Grafana Loki, or the self-provisioned fallback if the CKS infrastructure validation found Loki inaccessible for MaaS).\n- A running MaaS instance on CKS (from the CKS deployment validation) to collect logs from.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given the Authorino structured-logging configuration, when an authentication decision occurs (allow or deny), then the corresponding structured log entry reaches the log aggregation, measured by queries for Authorino's logs.\n- Given the Limitador structured-logging configuration, when a user exceeds a configured token rate limit, then the rate limit enforcement event (429 with exceeded quota) is retrievable from the log aggregation, measured by query.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P1] Observability logging functional: authentication events, rate limit enforcement, subscription selection (per Staff Engineer Input) — Authorino/Limitador logging configuration side (RHCL/OpenShift-owned)\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":43747,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a96c07aedf57c588","agent_id":"a43da7aa6bd0b6b38","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4feb-9959-cd45ee4b4e7a","uuid":"3c57e441-24b0-468b-9bde-650c737acddf","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:43:38.055Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Second revise RHAISTRAT-8003"}
