{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92a695dc6a02a4ef","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E003\n3\ttitle: MaaS 3.4 baseline feasibility investigation\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model as a Service\n6\tteam: MaaS\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: 0\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# MaaS 3.4 Baseline Feasibility Investigation\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves the unknowns about using the MaaS 3.4 GA codebase as the xKS Dev Preview baseline: stable/RC build availability, whether the Tenant CRD is frozen (blocking the configurable group claim path), and whether maas-api observability instrumentation can be added without conflicting with the 3.4 GA code freeze. All three questions are answered by inspecting the same artifact — the MaaS 3.4 GA/RC build and its repository — so they are combined into one investigation.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Confirm with the MaaS PM the latest date for a stable MaaS 3.4 build and whether an RC build is obtainable now (the strategy's mitigation: obtain RC by April 27 and begin CKS validation in parallel).\n34\t- Determine whether the Tenant CRD in MaaS 3.4 GA is frozen, i.e., whether adding a `groupClaimPath` field is possible within the release or requires a post-3.4 patch; if frozen, confirm the documented fallback (document the required OIDC claim format and push IdP configuration to customers). While inspecting the CRD, also verify the strategy's claim that the Tenant CRD carries external OIDC configuration fields (`oidcIssuerURL`, `oidcClientID`, `oidcAudience`) — architecture context does not confirm these fields, so the external-OIDC work treats them as unverified until this investigation checks the 3.4 baseline CRD spec.\n35\t- Determine whether maas-api Prometheus metrics instrumentation can be added without MaaS 3.4 GA code changes; if not, recommend post-3.4 patch vs deferral to P1 per the strategy's risk table.\n36\t- Produce a baseline feasibility report that downstream implementation epics build against.\n37\t\n38\t## Acceptance Criteria\n39\t\n40\t- A feasibility report exists identifying the concrete MaaS 3.4 build (GA or RC, with build identifier) to be used as the xKS Dev Preview baseline, or documenting the delay and the RC/fallback-demo plan if no stable build is available.\n41\t- The report states definitively whether the Tenant CRD can carry the configurable group claim path in the baseline, with the fallback documented if frozen, and whether the CRD carries the external OIDC configuration fields (`oidcIssuerURL`, `oidcClientID`, `oidcAudience`) the strategy claims.\n42\t- The report states definitively whether maas-api observability instrumentation is feasible in-tree for the baseline, with the post-3.4 patch or deferral recommendation if not.\n43\t\n44\t## HLR Traceability\n45\t\n46\t- [P0] Configurable OIDC group claim path mapping — feasibility gate\n47\t- [P0] Observability metrics functional — feasibility gate\n48\t- Dependency: MaaS 3.4 GA codebase (internal, \"critical blocker\" for Summit timeline)\n49\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd63816c50a5c19d","agent_id":"a76fca4762e0936a0","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4feb-9959-cd45ee4b4e7a","uuid":"2572768a-c177-4c91-9f27-048b1764a215","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:46:18.622Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-92a695dc6a02a4ef","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Final review RHAISTRAT-8003"}
