ocation) and its independence from OIDC/IdP availability\n51\t  - Group claim path configuration for non-standard claim formats (e.g., Entra ID `groups`, Cognito `cognito:groups`) and its effect on tier mapping\n52\t- Consolidated known-limitations topic drawing on the documented limitations and engineering delta from the CKS and AKS validation work.\n53\t- Content outline validated for technical accuracy against the implemented behavior and the architecture context (models-as-a-service.md).\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- A published documentation topic exists describing the user identity flow for xKS deployments, covering OIDC provider configuration, token flow, API key lifecycle, and group claim mapping.\n58\t- A known-limitations topic exists consolidating the CKS and AKS validation findings for MaaS on xKS versus RHOAI MaaS GA.\n59\t- Documentation is technically reviewed against the actual implementation (behavior verified on a deployed xKS MaaS instance) before publication.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- [P2] User identity flow documented for xKS deployments\n64\t- [P1] Known limitations documented (consolidation of validation deliverables)\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd63816c50a5c19d","agent_id":"a76fca4762e0936a0","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4feb-9959-cd45ee4b4e7a","uuid":"ff7dc061-b587-4368-9360-9a793a731226","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:46:40.765Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d8f69f0ffb5b571","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Final review RHAISTRAT-8003"}
