and the triggering identity), per the strategy's logging requirement.\n44\t- Log fields and labels formatted for aggregation in CKS Grafana Loki (label filters on identity, method, decision, reason per the strategy's logging acceptance criteria); the log-shipping/integration side is handled by the logging integration deliverable on xKS.\n45\t- If maas-api is frozen in the MaaS 3.4 GA baseline (resolved by the baseline feasibility investigation), deliver structured logging as a post-3.4 patch or defer this P1 scope per the strategy's risk table.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- Given structured logging enabled in maas-api, when an API key validation event occurs (success or failure), then the log entry is emitted as structured JSON including timestamp, user identity, authentication method, decision, and reason, measured by log inspection with label filters.\n50\t- Given structured logging enabled, when a subscription selection decision occurs, then the log entry records the selected subscription/tier and the triggering user identity, measured by log inspection.\n51\t- Log emission stays within the strategy's observability overhead budget (p99 5 ms threshold, async/post-response emission if exceeded), measured by latency benchmarking.\n52\t\n53\t## HLR Traceability\n54\t\n55\t- [P1] Observability logging functional: authentication events, rate limit enforcement, subscription selection (per Staff Engineer Input) — maas-api instrumentation side\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd63816c50a5c19d","agent_id":"a76fca4762e0936a0","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4feb-9959-cd45ee4b4e7a","uuid":"926c3358-2526-4782-9de8-ea8c7f1061a5","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:46:40.998Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ff66d89f2b63ab6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Final review RHAISTRAT-8003"}
