ry epic has testable Given/when/then acceptance criteria with explicit measurements. Rule-mandated ACs are present wherever applicable: E004 carries the build-pipeline-green AC (and RHOAI no-regression); E005 carries the backwards-compatibility/rollback-style AC (non-OIDC deployments retain KubernetesTokenReview behavior, verified by diff plus existing GA tests); E011 carries the technical-review-before-publication AC; E007/E008 carry the Kuadrant-mechanism AC covering investigation outcomes A/B. Failure-mode criteria from the strategy (IdP unavailability, Limitador termination, cert rotation, PostgreSQL unavailability) are distributed to the correct epics (E005, E007). No epic body references sibling epics by draft ID — cross-epic references use descriptive names (\"the baseline feasibility investigation\", \"the CKS infrastructure validation\"), which survive Jira creation. No vague or untestable ACs found.\n60\t\n61\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n62\tFull walk of the strategy against the epic set: all proposed happy-path and failure-mode acceptance criteria are covered (CKS/AKS deployment, API key persistence and use, 429 rate limiting, groupClaimPath tier mapping, known-limitations document, Prometheus metrics, Loki-retrievable structured logs, Perses dashboards, IdP-outage and Limitador-termination and cert-rotation and PostgreSQL-unavailability failure modes). All seven strategy open questions are carried into epic scope (stable build date → E003; RHCL commitment and official Helm charts → E001; shared/dedicated PostgreSQL → E004 as a chart value; OIDC caching → E005 with a dedicated AC; instrumentation feasibility → E003; CKS Prometheus/Loki → E002). All six risk-table mitigations are carried (RC-by-April-27 and 3.3 fallback demo as gate failure impacts, LRU cache as conditional scope on E005, p99 5ms overhead budget as ACs on E006/E013). Conditional branching is complete: outcomes A and B are correctly collapsed as structurally identical (chart provenance as an