uration | Implementation | RHCL / OpenShift | P1 |\n44\t| BRANCH-C-E012 | Contingency: direct Envoy ext_authz authentication and rate limiting | Implementation | MaaS | P0 |\n45\t\n46\tEpic count: 14 main-plan epics (15 including the branch contingency epic). E013 and E014 were split out of E006/E009 during revision so the P1 structured-logging scope is independently plannable/deferrable. E014 was further split during revision along the team line: the xKS-Platform-owned Loki integration (E014) is now separate from the RHCL/OpenShift-owned Authorino/Limitador logging configuration (E015) that the strategy's Affected Components table assigns to RHCL, so the xKS-owned integration no longer re-couples the external RHCL dependency.\n47\t\n48\t## Dependency DAG\n49\t\n50\t```mermaid\n51\tgraph TD\n52\t  E001 --> E005\n53\t  E001 --> E007\n54\t  E001 --> E008\n55\t  E002 --> E009\n56\t  E002 --> E014\n57\t  E003 --> E005\n58\t  E003 --> E006\n59\t  E003 --> E007\n60\t  E003 --> E013\n61\t  E004 --> E007\n62\t  E005 --> E007\n63\t  E006 --> E009\n64\t  E007 --> E008\n65\t  E007 --> E009\n66\t  E007 --> E010\n67\t  E007 --> E014\n68\t  E013 --> E014\n69\t  E014 --> E015\n70\t  E004 --> E011\n71\t  E005 --> E011\n72\t  E006 --> E011\n73\t  E007 --> E011\n74\t  E008 --> E011\n75\t  E009 --> E011\n76\t  E010 --> E011\n77\t  E013 --> E011\n78\t  E014 --> E011\n79\t  E015 --> E011\n80\t```\n81\t\n82\tRevision notes on the DAG: the redundant transitive edges E004→E008 and E005→E008 were removed (both already implied via E007, which the AKS validation consumes directly); E013/E014 carry the P1 logging scope split out of E006/E009; E015 carries the RHCL/OpenShift-owned Authorino/Limitador logging configuration split out of E014 along the team line. The E014/E015 split lengthens the documented critical path from 5 to 6 nodes (E001→E005→E007→E014→E015→E011) through the P1 logging chain; the P0/Summit-critical implementation path (E001→E005→E007→E008) is unchanged, and the P1 logging chain is independently deferrable per the strategy's risk table.\n83\t\n84\tBranch epic (not a main-plan node): `BRANCH-C-E012` depends on E001 (gated) and E004; selected only if the E001 investigation resolves to outcome C.\n85\t\n86\t## DAG Justification\n87\t\n88\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n89\t|------|------|-----------|\n90\t| E001 → E005 | 3 | Whether Kuadrant/Authorino is deployable on xKS determines whether the Authorino-based OIDC approach is viable at all; outcome C (Envoy ext_authz contingency) rewrites this epic's approach |\n91\t| E001 → E007 | 3 | The CKS validation epic deploys Kuadrant via the mechanism the investigation selects (RHCL Helm vs standalone vs contingency) — true gate, rewrite |\n92\t| E001 → E008 | 3 | Same gate applies to the AKS validation deployment |\n93\t| E002 → E009 | 3 | If CKS Prometheus is not accessible for MaaS, the observability integration approach changes (self-provisioned alternatives) — rewrite |\n94\t| E002 → E014 | 3 | If CKS Grafana Loki is not accessible for MaaS logs, the logging integration approach changes (self-provisioned alternative) — rewrite |\n95\t| E003 → E005 | 3 | Tenant CRD freeze status in MaaS 3.4 GA determines whether `groupClaimPath` is a code change or a documentation fallback — rewrite; E005 is gated by both the RHCL deployment path investigation and this investigation |\n96\t| E003 → E006 | 3 | maas-api instrumentation feasibility against the 3.4 GA code freeze determines in-tree vs post-3.4 patch vs deferral — rewrite |\n97\t| E003 → E007 | 3 | A usable 3.4 GA/RC baseline build is a precondition for CKS validation; if delayed, RC build or RHOAI 3.3 fallback demo is the remediation; E007 is gated by both the RHCL deployment path investigation and this investigation |\n98\t| E003 → E013 | 3 | maas-api freeze status determines whether structured logging is in-tree, a post-3.4 patch, or deferred — rewrite |\n99\t| E004 → E007 | 13 | The CKS validation deploys the Helm charts this epic produces — build-against artifact |\n100\t| E005 → E007 | 12 | CKS validation exercises the OIDC authentication and group claim mapping this epic delivers |\n101\t| E006 → E009 | 13 | Dashboards and Prometheus integration build against the metric names/contract this epic's instrumentation emits |\n102\t| E007 → E008 | strategy sequencing | Strategy and inline Staff Engineer Input mandate CKS-first validation; AKS validation consumes the CKS engineering delta and findings |\n103\t| E007 → E009 | 12/13 | Observability integration needs a running MaaS instance on CKS to scrape and query |\n104\t| E007 → E010 | 12 | Tracing validation needs the deployed request path (gateway → auth → payload-processing → backend) on CKS |\n105\t| E007 → E014 | 12/13 | Logging integration needs a running MaaS instance on CKS to collect logs from |\n106\t| E013 → E014 | 13 | Loki integration and label filters build against the structured log format/fields this epic's instrumentation emits |\n107\t| E007 → E015 | 12 | The Authorino/Limitador logging configuration is validated against a running MaaS instance on CKS |\n108\t| E014 → E015 | 13 | The Authorino/Limitador logs ship into the log-aggregation target (CKS Loki or the self-provisioned fallback) this epic delivers — build-against artifact; also carries the CKS infrastructure validation gate transitively to E015 |\n109\t| E004..E010, E013, E014, E015 → E011 | 11 | docs-authoring epic is blocked by all Implementation epics — docs describe what was built |\n110\t\n111\tRemoved during revision as redundant transitive edges: E004 → E008 and E005 → E008 (both implied via E007, which E008 directly consumes).\n112\t\n113\tNo edge between the two investigations and E004: Helm chart packaging of the MaaS components proceeds against the 3.4 RC build regardless of investigation outcomes (per the strategy's mitigation plan), and the chart itself is Kuadrant-mechanism-agnostic. No konflux-onboarding edges: the repo is already Konflux-built (architecture context