{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83b73973073d2996","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E015\n3\ttitle: Authorino and Limitador structured logging configuration\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Inference Gateway\n6\tteam: RHCL / OpenShift\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E007\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E014\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 0\n17\t  open_questions: 0\n18\t  external_dependency: -1\n19\t  human_process_gates: 0\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 0\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: Medium\n25\tai_implementability_score: 1\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Authorino and Limitador Structured Logging Configuration\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tConfigures structured logging for the Kuadrant components on the MaaS gateway path — Authorino (authentication decisions) and Limitador (rate limit enforcement) — so those events are captured and reach the xKS log aggregation. This work is owned by the RHCL/OpenShift team per the strategy's Affected Components table, which assigns the Authorino and Limitador logging configuration to RHCL/OpenShift (external). Split from the xKS-Platform-owned Loki integration so the external RHCL dependency is independently plannable: the Loki integration proceeds regardless of RHCL timing, and this epic ships its logs into whichever aggregation that integration delivers (CKS Grafana Loki or the self-provisioned fallback).\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Structured logging configuration for Authorino covering authentication decisions (identity, decision, reason), per the strategy's Affected Components and Impacted Teams tables: RHCL owns the logging configuration for these components, with the configuration guidance captured and applied on the xKS side.\n40\t- Structured logging configuration for Limitador covering rate limit enforcement events (429 with exceeded quota).\n41\t- Shipping the Authorino and Limitador structured logs into the log-aggregation deliverable (CKS Grafana Loki, or the self-provisioned fallback if the CKS infrastructure validation found Loki inaccessible for MaaS).\n42\t- A running MaaS instance on CKS (from the CKS deployment validation) to collect logs from.\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\t- Given the Authorino structured-logging configuration, when an authentication decision occurs (allow or deny), then the corresponding structured log entry reaches the log aggregation, measured by queries for Authorino's logs.\n47\t- Given the Limitador structured-logging configuration, when a user exceeds a configured token rate limit, then the rate limit enforcement event (429 with exceeded quota) is retrievable from the log aggregation, measured by query.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- [P1] Observability logging functional: authentication events, rate limit enforcement, subscription selection (per Staff Engineer Input) — Authorino/Limitador logging configuration side (RHCL/OpenShift-owned)\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-817539f93779a1be","agent_id":"a91a5677bf1f7de4b","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4feb-9959-cd45ee4b4e7a","uuid":"bb8e7fa5-1e3c-42c9-a183-6e74da1134a5","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:53:21.722Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-83b73973073d2996","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Third revise RHAISTRAT-8003"}
