{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba451702ec156191","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n3\ttitle: CKS observability infrastructure validation\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model and Agent Observability\n6\tteam: xKS Platform\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -2\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# CKS Observability Infrastructure Validation\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tValidates that CKS (CoreWeave Kubernetes Service) standard observability infrastructure is actually accessible and usable for MaaS: Prometheus scrape targets for MaaS metrics endpoints and Grafana Loki log aggregation with label filtering for MaaS namespaces. The strategy assumes both are available (\"CoreWeave standard infrastructure\") but flags the assumption as needing Sprint 1 validation; if either is inaccessible, the observability integration approach must change.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Confirm with the xKS Platform / CoreWeave side that the CKS Prometheus instance can scrape MaaS metrics endpoints (scrape target configuration, network reachability from the MaaS namespace).\n34\t- Confirm that CKS Grafana Loki ingests and aggregates logs from MaaS and Kuadrant namespaces and supports the label filters the strategy's logging acceptance criteria require (identity, method, decision, reason).\n35\t- Document access requirements, configuration steps, and any gaps discovered.\n36\t- Recommend the integration approach for the observability integration work, including a self-provisioned alternative if CKS infrastructure is not accessible.\n37\t\n38\t## Acceptance Criteria\n39\t\n40\t- A validation report exists stating whether CKS Prometheus can scrape a test metrics endpoint deployed in the MaaS namespace, measured by the metric appearing in a Prometheus query.\n41\t- The report states whether CKS Grafana Loki ingests structured JSON logs from the MaaS namespace with usable label filters, measured by a label-filtered Loki query returning a test log entry.\n42\t- If either capability is unavailable, the report specifies the fallback approach (e.g., self-provisioned Prometheus/Loki for the Dev Preview) and its implications.\n43\t\n44\t## HLR Traceability\n45\t\n46\t- [P0] Observability metrics functional: token usage, rate limiting enforcement, API key lifecycle events (per Staff Engineer Input) — prerequisite validation\n47\t- [P1] Observability logging functional: authentication events, rate limit enforcement, subscription selection (per Staff Engineer Input) — prerequisite validation\n48\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8e8b61976ffe5b4","agent_id":"aae76ed08c444b426","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4feb-9959-cd45ee4b4e7a","uuid":"33cdce2f-f628-4475-8c99-a023a85ad40c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:55:11.826Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba451702ec156191","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Post-revise review RHAISTRAT-8003"}
