{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2c761abc0fd2ce0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E014\n3\ttitle: Structured logging integration on xKS (Grafana Loki)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Model and Agent Observability\n6\tteam: xKS Platform\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E007\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E013\n13\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8003-E002\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If CKS Grafana Loki is not accessible for MaaS logs, self-provision\n17\t    the log aggregation for the Dev Preview per the validation report recommendation.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 0\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: -1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 0\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Medium\n31\tai_implementability_score: 1\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Structured Logging Integration on xKS: Grafana Loki\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tIntegrates the MaaS P1 structured-logging deliverable with the CKS log-aggregation stack: ships maas-api structured logs to CKS Grafana Loki with the label filters and queries supporting the strategy's logging acceptance criteria. Owned by the xKS Platform team. Split from the P0 metrics integration so the P1 logging scope can be deferred independently, and split from the Authorino/Limitador logging-configuration work (owned by RHCL/OpenShift per the strategy's Affected Components table) so the xKS-owned Loki integration is independently plannable from the external RHCL dependency.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Integration of maas-api structured logs with CKS Grafana Loki, building on the log format and labels emitted by the structured-logging instrumentation deliverable (identity, method, decision, reason).\n44\t- Log label filters and Loki queries supporting the strategy's logging acceptance criteria (timestamp, user identity, authentication method, decision, reason).\n45\t- A running MaaS instance on CKS (from the CKS deployment validation) to collect logs from.\n46\t- If the CKS infrastructure validation found Loki inaccessible for MaaS, implement the recommended fallback (e.g., a self-provisioned log-aggregation instance for the Dev Preview). The Authorino/Limitador structured-logging configuration is handled separately by the RHCL/OpenShift-owned logging-configuration epic, which ships its logs into the aggregation this epic delivers.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Given a deployed MaaS instance on CKS with structured logging enabled, when an authentication event occurs (success or failure) in maas-api, then the log entry is aggregated in CKS Grafana Loki and retrievable with label filters on timestamp, user identity, authentication method (OIDC/API key), decision (allow/deny), and reason (if denied), measured by querying CKS Grafana Loki.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- [P1] Observability logging functional: authentication events, rate limit enforcement, subscription selection (per Staff Engineer Input) — maas-api log aggregation side (Loki integration)\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8e8b61976ffe5b4","agent_id":"aae76ed08c444b426","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4feb-9959-cd45ee4b4e7a","uuid":"cc0a40ea-8144-4877-a54b-75840c26084f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:55:33.292Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2c761abc0fd2ce0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Post-revise review RHAISTRAT-8003"}
