{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87a0fe1f09f6ccdc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8003-E015\n3\ttitle: Authorino and Limitador structured logging configuration\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8003\n5\tcomponent: Inference Gateway\n6\tteam: RHCL / OpenShift\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8003-E014\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 0\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: -1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 0\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: Medium\n24\tai_implementability_score: 1\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Authorino and Limitador Structured Logging Configuration\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tConfigures structured logging for the Kuadrant components on the MaaS gateway path — Authorino (authentication decisions) and Limitador (rate limit enforcement) — so those events are captured and reach the xKS log aggregation. This work is owned by the RHCL/OpenShift team per the strategy's Affected Components table, which assigns the Authorino and Limitador logging configuration to RHCL/OpenShift (external). Split from the xKS-Platform-owned Loki integration so the external RHCL dependency is independently plannable: the Loki integration proceeds regardless of RHCL timing, and this epic ships its logs into whichever aggregation that integration delivers (CKS Grafana Loki or the self-provisioned fallback).\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Structured logging configuration for Authorino covering authentication decisions (identity, decision, reason), per the strategy's Affected Components and Impacted Teams tables: RHCL owns the logging configuration for these components, with the configuration guidance captured and applied on the xKS side.\n39\t- Structured logging configuration for Limitador covering rate limit enforcement events (429 with exceeded quota).\n40\t- Shipping the Authorino and Limitador structured logs into the log-aggregation deliverable (CKS Grafana Loki, or the self-provisioned fallback if the CKS infrastructure validation found Loki inaccessible for MaaS).\n41\t- A running MaaS instance on CKS (from the CKS deployment validation) to collect logs from.\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- Given the Authorino structured-logging configuration, when an authentication decision occurs (allow or deny), then the corresponding structured log entry reaches the log aggregation, measured by queries for Authorino's logs.\n46\t- Given the Limitador structured-logging configuration, when a user exceeds a configured token rate limit, then the rate limit enforcement event (429 with exceeded quota) is retrievable from the log aggregation, measured by query.\n47\t\n48\t## HLR Traceability\n49\t\n50\t- [P1] Observability logging functional: authentication events, rate limit enforcement, subscription selection (per Staff Engineer Input) — Authorino/Limitador logging configuration side (RHCL/OpenShift-owned)\n51\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8e8b61976ffe5b4","agent_id":"aae76ed08c444b426","session_id":"382ccfe0-6ddd-4feb-9959-cd45ee4b4e7a","uuid":"568a3aa7-2052-4ea0-ba1d-bc8a87c96c93","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:55:34.384Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-87a0fe1f09f6ccdc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Post-revise review RHAISTRAT-8003"}
